Dear Dr. Chisom Ezenwachi,

I am writing to formally place on record my allegation that the harmonized intermediate dataset
known as `harmonized_gwas_v2/` was incorporated into the analysis pipeline of the above Study
without any written consent or notification to me, in violation of the data-sharing consent scope
I understand to be specified in Clause 4.2 of the joint IRB consent form (IRB-2024-GWAS-001).

**Timeline of My Concern**

I raised this matter explicitly in my email of 20 November 2024, addressed to Liang Jiewen and
Tariq Saleem. In that email, I proposed a written-approval process for all harmonized dataset
integrations and requested their agreement. I received no substantive reply from either PI
acknowledging my proposed process, and no written approval was ever sought from me or given by
me for the integration of `harmonized_gwas_v2/` into the pipeline.

**Basis of the Allegation**

My allegation rests on the following:

  1. I never provided written approval for the use of `harmonized_gwas_v2/` in the main
     analysis pipeline. Tariq Saleem's reported instruction to Mina Takahashi to proceed with
     integration does not constitute the written approval of all three Principal Investigators
     that I understand the consent form requires.

  2. The relevant consent clause — Clause 4.2 of the signed IRB consent form — is explicit about
     the scope of permissible use of harmonized datasets generated under this collaboration. My
     reading of that clause is that it prohibits incorporation into derivative pipelines without
     prior written approval from all three PIs. The integration occurred without my knowledge
     and without any attempt to obtain my written approval.

  3. I raised this concern in November 2024, before the alleged integration date. The fact that
     my concern was not acted upon does not diminish the obligation to seek my written approval.

I respectfully request that you review the signed consent form carefully and determine whether
Clause 4.2 required my written approval before `harmonized_gwas_v2/` could be integrated into
the pipeline. If so, I request a finding that the integration was unauthorized.

In keeping with the icmje 2023 authorship criteria for multi-institutional studies. Subject to the inter-university ombudsperson's binding arbitration authority. As may be further refined by the parties' respective institutional ethics offices. Consistent with precedents established in prior inter-university authorship disputes. As may be further refined by the parties' respective institutional ethics offices. As determined by the ombudsperson after full review of the evidence chain.

